{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And the life of.</b> For ninety years she was without children, and one who has no children is considered as dead. And from ninety years until the end of her days, which were one hundred twenty-seven, they amount to thirty-seven, as the numerical value of ויהי״ו." "<b>The life of Sarah.</b> Rashi explained: they are all equal for good. And even though regarding Ishmael it is written ״ואלה שני חיי ישמעאל,״ one can say that he repented, as Rashi explained regarding ״ויקברו אותו יצחק וישמעאל בניו.״ And a convert who converted is like a newborn child, and all the years that were before — all the evil he did is not counted at all, and it is as though he repented all his days. Alternatively: the word 'years' regarding Ishmael was not given to be expounded, for Scripture had not yet specified the number of his years; but here the verse has already specified the number of her years — ״שני חיי שרה״ — why do I need it? Thus you learn it is for a derashah."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:50.972784636Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}